IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`

-- ccc20-part16-process.l4 -- sections 504 to 514 of the Criminal Code (Canada): information, summons and warrant. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text; nothing is claimed verified against the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a "may" whose gate is
-- "where", "when" or "upon" answers JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b), and is counted in the fork register as one of the readings left for a lawyer; a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE.
-- A duty is encoded as "the duty arises" (JUST TRUE) or "does not" (JUST FALSE). A rule of the form "shall X" without a named actor (505) is a decision function only: no actor is invented.

§ `Sections 504 to 506 -- Laying an information`

-- src:11231 | Information, Summons and Warrant
-- src:11232 | In what cases justice may receive information
-- src:11233 | 504 Any one who, on reasonable grounds, believes that a person has committed an indictable offence may lay an information in writing and under oath before a justice, and the justice shall receive the information, where it is alleged
-- src:11234 | (a) that the person has committed, anywhere, an indictable offence that may be tried in the province in which the justice resides, and that the person
-- src:11235 | (i) is or is believed to be, or
-- src:11236 | (ii) resides or is believed to reside,
-- src:11237 | within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice;
-- src:11238 | (b) that the person, wherever he may be, has committed an indictable offence within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice;
-- src:11239 | (c) that the person has, anywhere, unlawfully received property that was unlawfully obtained within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice; or
-- src:11240 | (d) that the person has in his possession stolen property within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice.
@ref s 504 (src:11231-11240)
GIVEN `the informant believes on reasonable grounds that the person has committed an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 504 any one may lay an information in writing and under oath before a justice` MEANS
    IF `the informant believes on reasonable grounds that the person has committed an indictable offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any one who, on reasonable grounds, believes that a person has committed an indictable offence may lay an information" (a "may" whose "if"-type gate fails)

@ref s 504 paragraphs (a) to (d) (src:11233-11240)
GIVEN `it is alleged that the person has committed, anywhere, an indictable offence that may be tried in the province in which the justice resides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is alleged that the person is or is believed to be, or resides or is believed to reside, within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is alleged that the person, wherever he may be, has committed an indictable offence within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is alleged that the person has, anywhere, unlawfully received property that was unlawfully obtained within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is alleged that the person has in his possession stolen property within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 504 the justice must receive the information` MEANS
    IF (`it is alleged that the person has committed, anywhere, an indictable offence that may be tried in the province in which the justice resides`
        AND `it is alleged that the person is or is believed to be, or resides or is believed to reside, within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice`)   -- (a)
       OR `it is alleged that the person, wherever he may be, has committed an indictable offence within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice`   -- (b)
       OR `it is alleged that the person has, anywhere, unlawfully received property that was unlawfully obtained within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice`   -- (c)
       OR `it is alleged that the person has in his possession stolen property within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice`   -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the justice shall receive the information, where it is alleged (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..."

-- 505: "an information ... shall be laid before a justice as soon as practicable after the issuance or release, and in any event before the time stated in the appearance notice or undertaking for their attendance
-- in court." The text names no actor who lays it, so this is a decision function over the facts and there is no regulative rule (no actor is invented).
-- src:11241 | Time within which information to be laid in certain cases
-- src:11242 | 505 If an appearance notice has been issued to an accused under section 497, or if an accused has been released from custody under section 498 or 503, an information relating to the offence alleged to have been committed by the accused or relating to an included or other offence alleged to have been committed by them shall be laid before a justice as soon as practicable after the issuance or release, and in any event before the time stated in the appearance notice or undertaking for their attendance in court.
@ref s 505 (src:11241-11242)
GIVEN `an appearance notice has been issued to the accused under section 497, or the accused has been released from custody under section 498 or 503` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 505 an information must be laid before a justice` MEANS
    IF `an appearance notice has been issued to the accused under section 497, or the accused has been released from custody under section 498 or 503`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appearance notice has been issued to an accused under section 497, or if an accused has been released from custody under section 498 or 503, an information ... shall be laid"

@ref s 505 (src:11242)
GIVEN `the information was laid as soon as practicable after the issuance or release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was laid before the time stated in the appearance notice or undertaking for the accused's attendance in court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 505 the information was laid in time` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid as soon as practicable after the issuance or release` AND `the information was laid before the time stated in the appearance notice or undertaking for the accused's attendance in court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable after the issuance or release, and in any event before the time stated in the appearance notice or undertaking for their attendance in court"

-- src:11243 | Form
-- src:11244 | 506 An information laid under section 504 or 505 may be in Form 2.
@ref s 506 (src:11243-11244)
GIVEN `the information is laid under section 504 or 505` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 506 the information may be in Form 2` MEANS
    IF `the information is laid under section 504 or 505`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An information laid under section 504 or 505 may be in Form 2" (a "may" for those informations only)

§ `Section 507 -- The justice hears the informant and witnesses: public prosecutions`

-- src:11245 | Justice to hear informant and witnesses — public prosecutions
-- src:11246 | 507 (1) Subject to subsection 523(1.1), a justice who receives an information laid under section 504 by a peace officer, a public officer, the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s agent, other than an information laid before the justice under section 505, shall, except if an accused has already been arrested with or without a warrant,
-- src:11247 | (a) hear and consider, ex parte,
-- src:11248 | (i) the allegations of the informant, and
-- src:11249 | (ii) the evidence of witnesses, where he considers it desirable or necessary to do so;
-- src:11250 | (a.1) if a hearing is held, hold it in camera; and
-- src:11251 | (b) where he considers that a case for so doing is made out, issue, in accordance with this section, either a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused to compel the accused to attend before him or some other justice for the same territorial division to answer to a charge of an offence.
@ref s 507(1) (src:11245-11251)
GIVEN `the information is laid under section 504 by a peace officer, a public officer, the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is one laid before the justice under section 505` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an accused has already been arrested with or without a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 523(1.1) provides that section 507 does not apply to the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(1) the justice must hear and consider the allegations of the informant and any evidence of witnesses, ex parte` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 523(1.1) provides that section 507 does not apply to the information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection 523(1.1)" (section 523(1.1): "section 507 or 508, as the case may be, does not apply in respect of the new information")
        IF NOT `the information is laid under section 504 by a peace officer, a public officer, the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a justice who receives an information laid under section 504 by a peace officer, a public officer, the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s agent ... shall"
        IF `the information is one laid before the justice under section 505` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an information laid before the justice under section 505"
        IF `an accused has already been arrested with or without a warrant` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except if an accused has already been arrested with or without a warrant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 507(1)(a.1) (src:11250)
GIVEN `a hearing is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(1)(a.1) the hearing must be held in camera` MEANS
    IF `a hearing is held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a.1) if a hearing is held, hold it in camera"

@ref s 507(1)(b) (src:11251)
GIVEN `the justice considers that a case for so doing is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(1)(b) the justice must issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the justice considers that a case for so doing is made out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where he considers that a case for so doing is made out, issue, in accordance with this section, either a summons or a warrant"

-- src:11252 | Process compulsory
-- src:11253 | (2) No justice shall refuse to issue a summons or warrant by reason only that the alleged offence is one for which a person may be arrested without warrant.
@ref s 507(2) (src:11252-11253)
GIVEN `the only reason for refusing is that the alleged offence is one for which a person may be arrested without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(2) the justice must not refuse to issue a summons or warrant` MEANS
    IF `the only reason for refusing is that the alleged offence is one for which a person may be arrested without warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No justice shall refuse to issue a summons or warrant by reason only that the alleged offence is one for which a person may be arrested without warrant" (the bar is limited to that one reason)

-- src:11254 | Procedure when witnesses attend
-- src:11255 | (3) A justice who hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1) shall
-- src:11256 | (a) take the evidence on oath; and
-- src:11257 | (b) cause the evidence to be taken in accordance with section 540 in so far as that section is capable of being applied.
@ref s 507(3) (src:11254-11257)
GIVEN `the justice hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(3) the justice must take the evidence on oath and in accordance with section 540` MEANS
    IF `the justice hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice who hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1) shall (a) take the evidence on oath; and (b) cause the evidence to be taken in accordance with section 540"

-- src:11258 | Summons to be issued except in certain cases
-- src:11259 | (4) Where a justice considers that a case is made out for compelling an accused to attend before him to answer to a charge of an offence, he shall issue a summons to the accused unless the allegations of the informant or the evidence of any witness or witnesses taken in accordance with subsection (3) discloses reasonable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused.
@ref s 507(4) (src:11258-11259)
GIVEN `the justice considers that a case is made out for compelling an accused to attend before the justice to answer to a charge of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allegations of the informant or the evidence taken disclose reasonable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(4) the justice must issue a summons to the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the justice considers that a case is made out for compelling an accused to attend before the justice to answer to a charge of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice considers that a case is made out for compelling an accused to attend before him to answer to a charge of an offence, he shall issue a summons"
        IF `the allegations of the informant or the evidence taken disclose reasonable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the allegations of the informant or the evidence of any witness or witnesses ... discloses reasonable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a warrant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11260 | No process in blank
-- src:11261 | (5) A justice shall not sign a summons or warrant in blank.
@ref s 507(5) (src:11260-11261)
GIVEN `the summons or warrant is blank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(5) the justice is barred from signing the summons or warrant` MEANS
    IF `the summons or warrant is blank`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice shall not sign a summons or warrant in blank" (a summons or warrant that is not blank is outside the bar)

-- src:11262 | Endorsement of warrant by justice
-- src:11263 | (6) A justice who issues a warrant under this section or section 508, 512, 512.1 or 512.2 may, unless the offence is one listed in section 469, authorize the release of the accused under section 499 by making an endorsement on the warrant in Form 29.
@ref s 507(6) (src:11262-11263)
GIVEN `the justice issues a warrant under section 507, 508, 512, 512.1 or 512.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(6) the justice may authorize the release of the accused under section 499 by endorsing the warrant in Form 29` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the justice issues a warrant under section 507, 508, 512, 512.1 or 512.2` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice who issues a warrant under this section or section 508, 512, 512.1 or 512.2 may"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the offence is one listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, unless the offence is one listed in section 469"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11264 | Undertaking or appearance notice deemed confirmed
-- src:11265 | (7) If, under subsection (6), a justice authorizes the release of an accused under section 499, an appearance notice or undertaking referred to in that section shall be deemed, for the purposes of subsection 145(3) or (4), as the case may be, to have been confirmed by a justice under section 508.
@ref s 507(7) (src:11264-11265)
GIVEN `the justice authorized the release of the accused under section 499 under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(7) the appearance notice or undertaking is deemed to have been confirmed by a justice under section 508` MEANS
    IF `the justice authorized the release of the accused under section 499 under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming is "for the purposes of subsection 145(3) or (4)" where a justice authorizes release under subsection (6); the text says nothing of any other case

-- src:11266 | Issue of summons or warrant
-- src:11267 | (8) Where, on an appeal from or review of any decision or matter of jurisdiction, a new trial or hearing or a continuance or renewal of a trial or hearing is ordered, a justice may issue either a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused in order to compel the accused to attend at the new or continued or renewed trial or hearing.
@ref s 507(8) (src:11266-11267)
GIVEN `on an appeal from or review of a decision or matter of jurisdiction, a new trial or hearing or a continuance or renewal of one is ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507(8) a justice may issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused to compel attendance` MEANS
    IF `on an appeal from or review of a decision or matter of jurisdiction, a new trial or hearing or a continuance or renewal of one is ordered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on an appeal from or review of any decision or matter of jurisdiction, a new trial or hearing ... is ordered, a justice may issue" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

§ `Section 507.1 -- Referral when private prosecution`

-- src:11268 | Referral when private prosecution
-- src:11269 | 507.1 (1) A justice who receives an information laid under section 504, other than an information referred to in subsection 507(1), shall refer it to a provincial court judge or, in Quebec, a judge of the Court of Quebec, or to a designated justice, to consider whether to compel the appearance of the accused on the information.
@ref s 507.1(1) (src:11268-11269)
GIVEN `the information is laid under section 504` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is one referred to in subsection 507(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(1) the justice must refer the information to a provincial court judge, a judge of the Court of Quebec or a designated justice` MEANS
    IF `the information is laid under section 504` AND NOT `the information is one referred to in subsection 507(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice who receives an information laid under section 504, other than an information referred to in subsection 507(1), shall refer it"

-- src:11270 | Summons or warrant
-- src:11271 | (2) A judge or designated justice to whom an information is referred under subsection (1) and who considers that a case for doing so is made out shall issue either a summons or warrant for the arrest of the accused to compel him or her to attend before a justice to answer to a charge of the offence charged in the information.
@ref s 507.1(2) (src:11270-11271)
GIVEN `the information was referred to the judge or designated justice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or designated justice considers that a case for doing so is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(2) the judge or designated justice must issue a summons or warrant for the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the information was referred to the judge or designated justice under subsection (1)` AND `the judge or designated justice considers that a case for doing so is made out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A judge or designated justice to whom an information is referred under subsection (1) and who considers that a case for doing so is made out shall issue"

-- src:11272 | Conditions for issuance
-- src:11273 | (3) The judge or designated justice may issue a summons or warrant only if he or she
-- src:11274 | (a) has heard and considered, ex parte and in camera, the allegations of the informant and the evidence of witnesses;
-- src:11275 | (b) is satisfied that the Attorney General has received a copy of the information;
-- src:11276 | (c) is satisfied that the Attorney General has received reasonable notice of the hearing under paragraph (a); and
-- src:11277 | (d) has given the Attorney General an opportunity to attend the hearing under paragraph (a) and to cross-examine and call witnesses and to present any relevant evidence at the hearing.
@ref s 507.1(3) (src:11272-11277)
GIVEN `the judge or designated justice has heard and considered, ex parte and in camera, the allegations of the informant and the evidence of witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or designated justice is satisfied that the Attorney General has received a copy of the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or designated justice is satisfied that the Attorney General has received reasonable notice of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or designated justice has given the Attorney General an opportunity to attend the hearing, to cross-examine and call witnesses and to present any relevant evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(3) the conditions for issuing a summons or warrant are all met` MEANS
    IF `the judge or designated justice has heard and considered, ex parte and in camera, the allegations of the informant and the evidence of witnesses`   -- (a)
       AND `the judge or designated justice is satisfied that the Attorney General has received a copy of the information`   -- (b)
       AND `the judge or designated justice is satisfied that the Attorney General has received reasonable notice of the hearing`   -- (c)
       AND `the judge or designated justice has given the Attorney General an opportunity to attend the hearing, to cross-examine and call witnesses and to present any relevant evidence`   -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The judge or designated justice may issue a summons or warrant only if he or she (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... and (d) ..."

-- src:11278 | Appearance of Attorney General
-- src:11279 | (4) The Attorney General may appear at the hearing held under paragraph (3)(a) without being deemed to intervene in the proceeding.
@ref s 507.1(4) (src:11278-11279)
GIVEN `the Attorney General appears at the hearing held under paragraph (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(4) the Attorney General is deemed to intervene in the proceeding by appearing at the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General appears at the hearing held under paragraph (3)(a)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Attorney General may appear at the hearing held under paragraph (3)(a) without being deemed to intervene in the proceeding"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection is about an appearance at the hearing; it says nothing of an Attorney General who does not appear

-- 507.1(5): an information not issued on: the judge or designated justice must endorse it. "Unless the informant, not later than six months after the endorsement, commences proceedings to compel the judge or designated
-- justice to issue a summons or warrant, the information is deemed never to have been laid." The six months are counted by month on the calendar (Date rolls an impossible day forward: fork F-month-end).
-- src:11280 | Information deemed not to have been laid
-- src:11281 | (5) If the judge or designated justice does not issue a summons or warrant under subsection (2), he or she shall endorse the information with a statement to that effect. Unless the informant, not later than six months after the endorsement, commences proceedings to compel the judge or designated justice to issue a summons or warrant, the information is deemed never to have been laid.
@ref s 507.1(5) (src:11280-11281)
GIVEN `the judge or designated justice does not issue a summons or warrant under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(5) the judge or designated justice must endorse the information with a statement to that effect` MEANS
    IF `the judge or designated justice does not issue a summons or warrant under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge or designated justice does not issue a summons or warrant under subsection (2), he or she shall endorse the information"

@ref s 507.1(5) the six months (src:11281)
GIVEN `the date of the endorsement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 507.1(5) the last day for commencing proceedings to compel` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the date of the endorsement`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of the endorsement` PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `the date of the endorsement`)

@ref s 507.1(5) (src:11281)
GIVEN `the date of the endorsement` IS A DATE
      `the informant commenced proceedings to compel the judge or designated justice to issue a summons or warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the informant commenced those proceedings` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the information is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(5) the information is deemed never to have been laid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the informant commenced proceedings to compel the judge or designated justice to issue a summons or warrant`
           AND `the date the informant commenced those proceedings` AT MOST (`s 507.1(5) the last day for commencing proceedings to compel` `the date of the endorsement`)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the informant, not later than six months after the endorsement, commences proceedings to compel the judge or designated justice to issue a summons or warrant"
        IF `the date on which the information is asked about` GREATER THAN (`s 507.1(5) the last day for commencing proceedings to compel` `the date of the endorsement`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): within the six months and no proceedings commenced yet, the text does not say how the matter stands

-- src:11282 | Information deemed not to have been laid — proceedings commenced
-- src:11283 | (6) If proceedings are commenced under subsection (5) and a summons or warrant is not issued as a result of those proceedings, the information is deemed never to have been laid.
@ref s 507.1(6) (src:11282-11283)
GIVEN `proceedings are commenced under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a summons or warrant is not issued as a result of those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(6) the information is deemed never to have been laid after the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `proceedings are commenced under subsection (5)` AND `a summons or warrant is not issued as a result of those proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming is for proceedings under subsection (5) that do not result in a summons or warrant; the text says nothing of the others

-- src:11284 | New evidence required for new hearing
-- src:11285 | (7) If a hearing in respect of an offence has been held under paragraph (3)(a) and the judge or designated justice has not issued a summons or a warrant, no other hearings may be held under that paragraph with respect to the offence or an included offence unless there is new evidence in support of the allegation in respect of which the hearing is sought to be held.
@ref s 507.1(7) (src:11284-11285)
GIVEN `a hearing in respect of the offence has been held under paragraph (3)(a) and the judge or designated justice has not issued a summons or a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is new evidence in support of the allegation in respect of which the hearing is sought to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(7) another hearing under paragraph (3)(a) on the offence or an included offence is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a hearing in respect of the offence has been held under paragraph (3)(a) and the judge or designated justice has not issued a summons or a warrant`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a hearing in respect of an offence has been held under paragraph (3)(a) and the judge or designated justice has not issued a summons or a warrant, no other hearings may be held"
        IF `there is new evidence in support of the allegation in respect of which the hearing is sought to be held` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless there is new evidence in support of the allegation in respect of which the hearing is sought to be held"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11286 | Subsections 507(2) to (8) to apply
-- src:11287 | (8) Subsections 507(2) to (8) apply to proceedings under this section.
@ref s 507.1(8) (src:11286-11287)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 507.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(8) subsections 507(2) to (8) apply` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 507.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection applies subsections 507(2) to (8) to proceedings under this section and says nothing of other proceedings

-- src:11288 | Non-application — informations laid under sections 810, 810.03 and 810.1
-- src:11289 | (9) Subsections (1) to (8) do not apply in respect of an information laid under section 810, 810.03 or 810.1.
@ref s 507.1(9) (src:11288-11289)
GIVEN `the information is laid under section 810, 810.03 or 810.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(9) subsections (1) to (8) apply to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information is laid under section 810, 810.03 or 810.1`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) to (8) do not apply in respect of an information laid under section 810, 810.03 or 810.1"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only that they do not apply to those informations

-- src:11290 | Definition of designated justice
-- src:11291 | (10) In this section, designated justice means a justice designated for the purpose by the chief judge of the provincial court having jurisdiction in the matter or, in Quebec, a justice designated by the chief judge of the Court of Quebec.
@ref s 507.1(10) (src:11290-11291)
GIVEN `the matter is in Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is designated for the purpose by the chief judge of the provincial court having jurisdiction in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is designated for the purpose by the chief judge of the Court of Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(10) the justice is a designated justice` MEANS
    IF `the matter is in Quebec`
    THEN (IF `the justice is designated for the purpose by the chief judge of the Court of Quebec` THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "designated justice means ... in Quebec, a justice designated by the chief judge of the Court of Quebec"
    ELSE (IF `the justice is designated for the purpose by the chief judge of the provincial court having jurisdiction in the matter` THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "designated justice means a justice designated for the purpose by the chief judge of the provincial court having jurisdiction in the matter"

-- src:11292 | Meaning of Attorney General
-- src:11293 | (11) In this section, Attorney General includes the Attorney General of Canada and his or her lawful deputy in respect of proceedings that could have been commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government.
@ref s 507.1(11) (src:11292-11293)
GIVEN `the person is the Attorney General as section 2 defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General's lawful deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings could have been commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 507.1(11) the person is the Attorney General for the purposes of section 507.1` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Attorney General as section 2 defines the term`
       OR (`the person is the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General's lawful deputy`
           AND `the proceedings could have been commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, Attorney General includes the Attorney General of Canada and his or her lawful deputy in respect of proceedings that could have been commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada"

§ `Section 508 -- The justice hears the informant and witnesses: informations laid under section 505`

-- src:11294 | Justice to hear informant and witnesses
-- src:11295 | 508 (1) A justice who receives an information laid before him under section 505 shall
-- src:11296 | (a) hear and consider, ex parte,
-- src:11297 | (i) the allegations of the informant, and
-- src:11298 | (ii) the evidence of witnesses, where he considers it desirable or necessary to do so;
-- src:11299 | (a.1) if a hearing is held, hold it in camera;
@ref s 508(1)(a) and (a.1) (src:11294-11299)
GIVEN `the information was laid before the justice under section 505` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(1) the justice must hear and consider the allegations of the informant and any evidence of witnesses, ex parte` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid before the justice under section 505`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice who receives an information laid before him under section 505 shall"

@ref s 508(1)(a.1) (src:11299)
GIVEN `a hearing is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(1)(a.1) the hearing must be held in camera` MEANS
    IF `a hearing is held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a.1) if a hearing is held, hold it in camera"

-- src:11300 | (b) if the justice considers that a case for so doing is made out, whether the information relates to the offence alleged in the appearance notice or undertaking or to an included or other offence,
-- src:11301 | (i) confirm the appearance notice or undertaking and endorse the information accordingly,
-- src:11302 | (ii) cancel the appearance notice or undertaking and issue, in accordance with section 507, either a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused to compel the accused to attend before the justice or some other justice for the same territorial division to answer to a charge of an offence and endorse on the summons or warrant that the appearance notice or undertaking has been cancelled, or
-- src:11303 | (iii) in the case of the undertaking, amend it to correct the time and place set out in the condition requiring the accused to attend court; and
-- src:11304 | (c) if the justice considers that a case is not made out for the purposes of paragraph (b), cancel the appearance notice or undertaking and cause the accused to be immediately notified of the cancellation.
@ref s 508(1)(b) and (c) (src:11300-11304)
DECLARE `s 508(1)(b) what the justice does` IS ONE OF
    `s 508(1)(b)(i) confirm the appearance notice or undertaking and endorse the information accordingly`
    `s 508(1)(b)(ii) cancel the appearance notice or undertaking and issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused, and endorse that it has been cancelled`
    `s 508(1)(b)(iii) amend the undertaking to correct the time and place set out in the condition requiring the accused to attend court`

@ref s 508(1)(b) (src:11300-11303)
GIVEN `the justice considers that a case for so doing is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `s 508(1)(b) what the justice does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(1)(b) the justice must take that step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the justice considers that a case for so doing is made out` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the justice considers that a case for so doing is made out"
        IF step EQUALS `s 508(1)(b)(iii) amend the undertaking to correct the time and place set out in the condition requiring the accused to attend court` AND NOT `the document is an undertaking`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(iii) in the case of the undertaking, amend it"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- one of (i), (ii) or (iii)

@ref s 508(1)(c) (src:11304)
GIVEN `the justice considers that a case is not made out for the purposes of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(1)(c) the justice must cancel the appearance notice or undertaking and cause the accused to be immediately notified` MEANS
    IF `the justice considers that a case is not made out for the purposes of paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) if the justice considers that a case is not made out for the purposes of paragraph (b), cancel the appearance notice or undertaking"

-- src:11305 | Procedure when witnesses attend
-- src:11306 | (2) A justice who hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1) shall
-- src:11307 | (a) take the evidence on oath; and
-- src:11308 | (b) cause the evidence to be taken in accordance with section 540 in so far as that section is capable of being applied.
@ref s 508(2) (src:11305-11308)
GIVEN `the justice hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508(2) the justice must take the evidence on oath and in accordance with section 540` MEANS
    IF `the justice hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice who hears the evidence of a witness pursuant to subsection (1) shall (a) take the evidence on oath"

-- src:11309 | Information laid otherwise than in person
-- src:11310 | 508.1 (1) For the purposes of sections 504 to 508, a peace officer may lay an information by any means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
-- src:11311 | Alternative to oath
-- src:11312 | (2) A peace officer who uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (1) shall, instead of swearing an oath, make a statement in writing stating that all matters contained in the information are true to the officer’s knowledge and belief, and such a statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath.
@ref s 508.1 (src:11309-11312)
GIVEN `the information is laid for the purposes of sections 504 to 508 by a peace officer by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508.1(1) the peace officer may lay the information by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `the information is laid for the purposes of sections 504 to 508 by a peace officer by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a peace officer may lay an information by any means of telecommunication that produces a writing" (a "may" limited to a peace officer and to a means that produces a writing)

@ref s 508.1(2) (src:11312)
GIVEN `the peace officer used a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer made a statement in writing stating that all matters contained in the information are true to the officer's knowledge and belief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 508.1(2) the statement in writing is deemed to be a statement made under oath` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer used a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (1)` AND `the peace officer made a statement in writing stating that all matters contained in the information are true to the officer's knowledge and belief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such a statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath" (the deeming is for that statement made by a peace officer who used a means of telecommunication)

§ `Sections 509 to 511 -- Summons and warrant: contents, service and effect`

-- src:11313 | Summons
-- src:11314 | 509 (1) A summons issued under this Part shall
-- src:11315 | (a) be directed to the accused;
-- src:11316 | (b) set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged; and
-- src:11317 | (c) require the accused to attend court at a time and place to be stated therein and to attend thereafter as required by the court in order to be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 509(1) (src:11313-11317)
GIVEN `the summons is directed to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons sets out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons requires the accused to attend court at a time and place stated in it and to attend thereafter as required by the court in order to be dealt with according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 509(1) the summons meets the requirements of paragraphs (a) to (c)` MEANS
    IF `the summons is directed to the accused` AND `the summons sets out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged`
       AND `the summons requires the accused to attend court at a time and place stated in it and to attend thereafter as required by the court in order to be dealt with according to law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A summons issued under this Part shall (a) be directed to the accused; (b) set out briefly the offence ...; and (c) require the accused to attend court"

-- 509 (2) A summons shall be served by a peace officer who shall deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found, shall leave it for him at his latest or usual
-- place of abode with an inmate thereof who appears to be at least sixteen years of age. (3) is repealed.
-- src:11318 | Service on individual
-- src:11319 | (2) A summons shall be served by a peace officer who shall deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found, shall leave it for him at his latest or usual place of abode with an inmate thereof who appears to be at least sixteen years of age.
@ref s 509(2) (src:11318-11319)
GIVEN `the summons is served by a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer delivers it personally to the person to whom it is directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom it is directed cannot conveniently be found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer leaves it at the person's latest or usual place of abode with an inmate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the apparent age in years of the inmate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 509(2) the summons has been served as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the summons is served by a peace officer` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A summons shall be served by a peace officer"
        IF `the peace officer delivers it personally to the person to whom it is directed` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person to whom it is directed cannot conveniently be found` AND `the peace officer leaves it at the person's latest or usual place of abode with an inmate` AND `the apparent age in years of the inmate` AT LEAST 16 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found, shall leave it for him at his latest or usual place of abode with an inmate thereof who appears to be at least sixteen years of age"

-- src:11322 | (4) The summons must set out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2).
@ref s 509(4) (src:11322)
GIVEN `the summons sets out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 509(4) the summons sets out the required summary` MEANS
    IF `the summons sets out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The summons must set out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)"

-- src:11323 | Attendance for purposes of Identification of Criminals Act
-- src:11324 | (5) A summons may require the accused to appear at a time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, if the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act.
@ref s 509(5) (src:11323-11324)
GIVEN `the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 509(5) the summons may require the accused to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    IF `the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11326 | Contents of warrant to arrest
-- src:11327 | 511 (1) A warrant issued under this Part shall
-- src:11328 | (a) name or describe the accused;
-- src:11329 | (b) set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged; and
-- src:11330 | (c) order that the accused be forthwith arrested and brought before the judge or justice who issued the warrant or before some other judge or justice having jurisdiction in the same territorial division, to be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 511(1) (src:11326-11330)
GIVEN `the warrant names or describes the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant sets out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant orders that the accused be forthwith arrested and brought before the judge or justice who issued the warrant or before some other judge or justice having jurisdiction in the same territorial division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(1) the warrant meets the requirements of paragraphs (a) to (c)` MEANS
    IF `the warrant names or describes the accused` AND `the warrant sets out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged`
       AND `the warrant orders that the accused be forthwith arrested and brought before the judge or justice who issued the warrant or before some other judge or justice having jurisdiction in the same territorial division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A warrant issued under this Part shall (a) name or describe the accused; (b) set out briefly the offence ...; and (c) order that the accused be forthwith arrested"

-- src:11331 | No return day
-- src:11332 | (2) A warrant issued under this Part remains in force until it is executed and need not be made returnable at any particular time.
@ref s 511(2) (src:11331-11332)
GIVEN `the warrant has been executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(2) the warrant remains in force` MEANS
    IF `the warrant has been executed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A warrant issued under this Part remains in force until it is executed" (an "until" bar: after execution it is no longer in force under this subsection)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:11333 | Warrant — cancellation
-- src:11334 | (2.1) Despite subsection (2), a judge or justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued may cancel the warrant on application by the prosecutor, with or without the appearance of the accused, if the judge or justice is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to do so.
@ref s 511(2.1) (src:11333-11334)
GIVEN `the judge or justice has jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to cancel the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(2.1) the judge or justice may cancel the warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may cancel the warrant on application by the prosecutor" (an "on" gate on a "may": the delegated ruling (c) counts "upon" as "where"; the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)
        IF NOT (`the judge or justice has jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued` AND `the judge or justice is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to cancel the warrant`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judge or justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued may cancel the warrant on application by the prosecutor, ... if the judge or justice is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to do so" (a "may" whose scope limit or "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11335 | Discretion to postpone execution
-- src:11336 | (3) Notwithstanding paragraph (1)(c), a judge or justice who issues a warrant may specify in the warrant the period before which the warrant shall not be executed, to allow the accused to appear voluntarily before a judge or justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued.
@ref s 511(3) (src:11335-11336)
GIVEN `the judge or justice issues the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is specified to allow the accused to appear voluntarily before a judge or justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(3) the judge or justice may specify a period before which the warrant shall not be executed` MEANS
    IF `the judge or justice issues the warrant` AND `the period is specified to allow the accused to appear voluntarily before a judge or justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the warrant was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judge or justice who issues a warrant may specify in the warrant the period before which the warrant shall not be executed, to allow the accused to appear voluntarily" (a "may" limited to that purpose)

-- src:11337 | Deemed execution of warrant
-- src:11338 | (4) Where the accused appears voluntarily for the offence in respect of which the accused is charged, the warrant is deemed to be executed.
@ref s 511(4) (src:11337-11338)
GIVEN `the accused appears voluntarily for the offence in respect of which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(4) the warrant is deemed to be executed` MEANS
    IF `the accused appears voluntarily for the offence in respect of which the accused is charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the accused appears voluntarily for the offence in respect of which the accused is charged, the warrant is deemed to be executed" (a "where" condition failing: ruling (b))

§ `Sections 512 to 514 -- Issuing, directing and executing a summons or warrant`

-- 512 (1): "notwithstanding that (a) ... (b) ... (c) ...": each is a prior step that does not stop the justice from issuing a summons or warrant. The list is not closed by "only".
-- src:11339 | Certain actions not to preclude issue of warrant
-- src:11340 | 512 (1) A justice may, where the justice has reasonable and probable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused, issue a summons or warrant, notwithstanding that
-- src:11341 | (a) an appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed or cancelled under subsection 508(1);
-- src:11342 | (b) a summons has previously been issued under subsection 507(4); or
-- src:11343 | (c) the accused has been released without conditions or with the intention of compelling their appearance by way of summons.
@ref s 512(1) (src:11339-11343)
DECLARE `s 512(1) a prior step` IS ONE OF
    `s 512(1)(a) an appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed or cancelled under subsection 508(1)`
    `s 512(1)(b) a summons has previously been issued under subsection 507(4)`
    `s 512(1)(c) the accused has been released without conditions or with the intention of compelling their appearance by way of summons`
    `s 512(1) a prior step the text does not name`

@ref s 512(1) (src:11340-11343)
GIVEN `the justice has reasonable and probable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `s 512(1) a prior step`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 512(1) the justice may issue a summons or warrant notwithstanding the prior step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the justice has reasonable and probable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice may, where the justice has reasonable and probable grounds to believe that it is necessary in the public interest to issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused, issue a summons or warrant" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)
        IF step EQUALS `s 512(1) a prior step the text does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "notwithstanding that (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (the text names three prior steps and does not say "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11344 | Warrant in default of appearance
-- src:11345 | (2) Where
-- src:11346 | (a) service of a summons is proved and the accused fails to attend court in accordance with the summons,
-- src:11347 | (b) an appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed under subsection 508(1) and the accused fails to attend court in accordance with it in order to be dealt with according to law, or
-- src:11348 | (c) it appears that a summons cannot be served because the accused is evading service,
-- src:11349 | a justice may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused.
@ref s 512(2) (src:11344-11349)
GIVEN `service of a summons is proved and the accused fails to attend court in accordance with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed under subsection 508(1) and the accused fails to attend court in accordance with it in order to be dealt with according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that a summons cannot be served because the accused is evading service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 512(2) a justice may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    IF `service of a summons is proved and the accused fails to attend court in accordance with the summons`   -- (a)
       OR `an appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed under subsection 508(1) and the accused fails to attend court in accordance with it in order to be dealt with according to law`   -- (b)
       OR `it appears that a summons cannot be served because the accused is evading service`   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where (a) service of a summons is proved and the accused fails to attend ..., (b) ..., or (c) ..., a justice may issue a warrant" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

-- src:11350 | Arrest warrant — failure to appear under summons
-- src:11351 | 512.1 If an accused who is required by a summons to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act does not appear at that time and place and, in the case of an offence designated as a contravention under the Contraventions Act, the Attorney General, within the meaning of that Act, has not made an election under section 50 of that Act, a justice may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused for the offence with which the accused is charged.
@ref s 512.1 (src:11350-11351)
GIVEN `the accused is required by a summons to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act and does not appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is designated as a contravention under the Contraventions Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General within the meaning of that Act has made an election under section 50 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 512.1 a justice may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the accused is required by a summons to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act and does not appear`
       AND NOT (`the offence is designated as a contravention under the Contraventions Act` AND `the Attorney General within the meaning of that Act has made an election under section 50 of that Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused who is required by a summons to appear ... does not appear at that time and place and, in the case of an offence designated as a contravention under the Contraventions Act, the Attorney General ... has not made an election under section 50 of that Act, a justice may issue a warrant" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11352 | Arrest warrant — failure to appear under appearance notice or undertaking
-- src:11353 | 512.2 If an accused who is required by an appearance notice or undertaking to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act does not appear at that time and place, a justice may, if the appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed by a justice under section 508, issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused for the offence with which the accused is charged.
@ref s 512.2 (src:11352-11353)
GIVEN `the accused is required by an appearance notice or undertaking to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act and does not appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed by a justice under section 508` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 512.2 a justice may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the accused is required by an appearance notice or undertaking to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act and does not appear`
       AND `the appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed by a justice under section 508`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused who is required by an appearance notice or undertaking to appear ... does not appear at that time and place, a justice may, if the appearance notice or undertaking has been confirmed by a justice under section 508, issue a warrant" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11354 | Warrant to appear under section 524
-- src:11355 | 512.3 If a justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an accused has contravened or is about to contravene any summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order that was issued or given to the accused or entered into by the accused or has committed an offence while being subject to any summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order, the justice may issue a warrant for the purpose of taking the accused before a justice under section 524.
@ref s 512.3 (src:11354-11355)
GIVEN `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or is about to contravene a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has committed an offence while subject to a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 512.3 a justice may issue a warrant to take the accused before a justice under section 524` MEANS
    IF `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or is about to contravene a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order`
       OR `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has committed an offence while subject to a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe ... the justice may issue a warrant" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11356 | Formalities of warrant
-- src:11357 | 513 A warrant in accordance with this Part shall be directed to the peace officers within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which it is issued.
@ref s 513 (src:11356-11357)
GIVEN `the warrant is directed to the peace officers within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 513 the warrant is directed as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is directed to the peace officers within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A warrant in accordance with this Part shall be directed to the peace officers within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which it is issued"

-- src:11358 | Execution of warrant
-- src:11359 | 514 (1) A warrant in accordance with this Part may be executed by arresting the accused
-- src:11360 | (a) wherever he is found within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which the warrant was issued; or
-- src:11361 | (b) wherever he is found in Canada, in the case of fresh pursuit.
@ref s 514(1) (src:11358-11361)
GIVEN `the accused is found within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is found elsewhere in Canada, in the case of fresh pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 514(1) the warrant may be executed by arresting the accused where the accused is found` MEANS
    IF `the accused is found within the territorial jurisdiction of the justice, judge or court by whom or by which the warrant was issued` OR `the accused is found elsewhere in Canada, in the case of fresh pursuit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant in accordance with this Part may be executed by arresting the accused (a) wherever he is found within the territorial jurisdiction ...; or (b) wherever he is found in Canada, in the case of fresh pursuit" (a "may" whose limbs are not met)

-- src:11362 | By whom warrant may be executed
-- src:11363 | (2) A warrant in accordance with this Part may be executed by a person who is one of the peace officers to whom it is directed, whether or not the place in which the warrant is to be executed is within the territory for which the person is a peace officer.
@ref s 514(2) (src:11362-11363)
GIVEN `the person is one of the peace officers to whom the warrant is directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 514(2) the person may execute the warrant, whether or not the place is within the territory for which the person is a peace officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is one of the peace officers to whom the warrant is directed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be executed by a person who is one of the peace officers to whom it is directed" (a "may" limited to those peace officers)
